cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper listed under preferred-citation."
title: "Amanah: reference implementation and specification of the Portable Clinical Obligation"
abstract: >-
  Amanah is a free, open-source registry for portable clinical obligations: patient-held records of
  a clinician-recommended follow-up, tracked until evidence shows it happened. It detects no disease
  and makes no diagnostic claim. It carries detections that have already been made through to the
  treatment that should have followed. This repository holds the Portable Clinical Obligation
  specification, the concept note, and the naming policy.
